---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — CardHearth';
const description =
  'CardHearth privacy policy: what we store (your game data, on your device), the analytics and advertising services we use, optional accounts, and how to contact us.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="mx-auto flex min-h-dvh w-full max-w-2xl flex-col px-4">
    <header class="py-10">
      <p class="text-sm font-bold opacity-70"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">← CardHearth</a></p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Last updated: June 12, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <section class="text-sm leading-relaxed opacity-90">
      <h2 class="mb-2 mt-4 text-lg font-bold">What we store on your device</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        CardHearth saves your in-progress games, settings (theme, card backs, sound preferences,
        and similar), and play statistics (games played, wins, streaks, best times) in your
        browser's local storage. This data stays on your device — it is not transmitted to us
        and is not linked to your identity — unless you choose to sign in and sync it (see
        "Optional accounts" below). You can erase it at any time by clearing your browser's
        site data for cardhearth.com.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mb-2 mt-4 text-lg font-bold">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        We use two analytics services to understand how the site is used — which games people
        enjoy, and where things break. <strong>Google Analytics</strong> collects standard usage
        data (pages visited, approximate location, device and browser type) using cookies.
        <strong>Ahrefs Analytics</strong> is cookieless and gives us only aggregate counts.
        Neither tells us who you are, and we don't use them for anything else.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Advertising keeps the site free. We use <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, which loads its
        own script and may set advertising cookies to measure ads and — where permitted —
        personalize them. Where the law requires it, you will be asked for consent before any
        advertising cookies are set, and you can decline personalized ads there or in your
        Google ad settings at any time.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-3">
        If you turn on the optional daily-reminder notification, we store the web push endpoint
        your browser gives us, plus your chosen reminder hour and timezone — enough to send the
        reminder, and not linked to your identity. Turning the reminder off removes it.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mb-2 mt-4 text-lg font-bold">Optional accounts</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        You can play everything as a guest with no account. If you choose to sign in (with
        Google) to sync your progress across devices, we store only your account's email address
        and your game progress (stats, streaks, and badges) — nothing else. We never post
        anything, never contact you without asking, and you can sign out or request deletion of
        your synced data at any time by emailing us. Guest play remains fully available and
        unaffected.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mb-2 mt-4 text-lg font-bold">Children</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        CardHearth is a general-audience site and does not knowingly collect personal
        information from children.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mb-2 mt-4 text-lg font-bold">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a class="underline" href="mailto:hello@cardhearth.com">hello@cardhearth.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>
